WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.524
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Sarah. Welcome to Online Proficiency.

2
00:00:05.824 --> 00:00:08.955
Hi! I'm Rithy. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.255 --> 00:00:17.689
Unit thirty-two: Nature and the Sacred. In this unit, you will report and attribute views on sacred nature accurately.

4
00:00:18.683 --> 00:00:19.905
sacred grove.

5
00:00:20.605 --> 00:00:26.320
sacred grove means a group of trees protected for religious or spiritual reasons.

6
00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:29.397
The village sacred grove has never been cut.

7
00:00:30.097 --> 00:00:33.156
Your turn. Say: sacred grove.

8
00:00:35.856 --> 00:00:37.194
sacred grove.

9
00:00:38.183 --> 00:00:39.475
spirit forest.

10
00:00:40.175 --> 00:00:45.460
spirit forest means a forest believed to be home to ancestral or guardian spirits.

11
00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:49.118
The Bunong protect their spirit forest in Mondulkiri.

12
00:00:49.818 --> 00:00:53.283
Your turn. Say: spirit forest.

13
00:00:55.983 --> 00:00:57.379
spirit forest.

14
00:00:58.383 --> 00:00:59.338
animism.

15
00:01:00.038 --> 00:01:06.031
animism means the belief that natural things such as rivers, trees and mountains have spirits.

16
00:01:06.331 --> 00:01:09.980
Animism shaped Khmer beliefs long before Buddhism arrived.

17
00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:13.576
Your turn. Say: animism.

18
00:01:16.276 --> 00:01:17.288
animism.

19
00:01:18.283 --> 00:01:20.294
ecological spirituality.

20
00:01:20.994 --> 00:01:26.628
ecological spirituality means a spiritual sense of connection with the natural world.

21
00:01:26.928 --> 00:01:31.006
Ecological spirituality inspires monks who ordain trees.

22
00:01:31.706 --> 00:01:35.589
Your turn. Say: ecological spirituality.

23
00:01:38.289 --> 00:01:40.381
ecological spirituality.

24
00:01:41.383 --> 00:01:42.814
reverence for nature.

25
00:01:43.514 --> 00:01:48.126
reverence for nature means deep respect and awe towards the natural world.

26
00:01:48.426 --> 00:01:51.969
Reverence for nature can be a powerful conservation tool.

27
00:01:52.669 --> 00:01:55.740
Your turn. Say: reverence for nature.

28
00:01:58.440 --> 00:01:59.882
reverence for nature.

29
00:02:00.883 --> 00:02:02.221
sacred mountain.

30
00:02:02.921 --> 00:02:07.010
sacred mountain means a mountain considered holy by a community.

31
00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:11.098
Phnom Kulen is a sacred mountain for many Cambodians.

32
00:02:11.798 --> 00:02:14.799
Your turn. Say: sacred mountain.

33
00:02:17.499 --> 00:02:18.767
sacred mountain.

34
00:02:19.783 --> 00:02:21.527
indigenous cosmology.

35
00:02:22.227 --> 00:02:29.486
indigenous cosmology means an indigenous people's understanding of the universe and humanity's place in it.

36
00:02:29.786 --> 00:02:34.735
In their indigenous cosmology, the forest and the village are one community.

37
00:02:35.435 --> 00:02:38.784
Your turn. Say: indigenous cosmology.

38
00:02:41.484 --> 00:02:43.239
indigenous cosmology.

39
00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:45.948
biocultural diversity.

40
00:02:46.648 --> 00:02:53.802
biocultural diversity means the link between the variety of life and the variety of cultures and languages.

41
00:02:54.102 --> 00:02:58.261
Losing a language can also mean losing biocultural diversity.

42
00:02:58.961 --> 00:03:02.531
Your turn. Say: biocultural diversity.

43
00:03:05.231 --> 00:03:06.975
biocultural diversity.

44
00:03:07.983 --> 00:03:10.134
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:03:10.434 --> 00:03:15.243
Rithy, I read that some forests in Cambodia survive because they are sacred.

46
00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:22.488
Yes. Researchers have found that spirit forests are often better preserved than ordinary ones.

47
00:03:23.783 --> 00:03:25.191
Who reported that?

48
00:03:26.483 --> 00:03:32.314
Several conservation studies; according to one, sacred groves protect rare species.

49
00:03:33.617 --> 00:03:36.150
And what do the communities themselves say?

50
00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:42.491
Bunong elders insist that cutting a spirit forest would anger the ancestors.

51
00:03:43.783 --> 00:03:46.642
Some scientists dismiss that as superstition.

52
00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:52.481
Others acknowledge that reverence for nature may achieve what laws alone cannot.

53
00:03:53.783 --> 00:03:58.581
Grammar focus: Precise reporting and attribution (extended).

54
00:03:58.881 --> 00:04:01.914
Reporting verbs show your attitude to a source.

55
00:04:02.214 --> 00:04:09.243
Researchers have found that spirit forests are better preserved. Bunong elders insist that cutting them would anger the ancestors.

56
00:04:09.543 --> 00:04:13.714
Some scientists dismiss this; others acknowledge its value.

57
00:04:14.014 --> 00:04:21.389
Choose reporting verbs carefully: 'claim' and 'dismiss' signal doubt, while 'show' and 'acknowledge' signal acceptance.

58
00:04:22.383 --> 00:04:25.593
Now read and listen. Where Forests Are Holy.

59
00:04:25.893 --> 00:04:32.293
Across Asia and Africa, communities protect sacred groves where cutting trees is forbidden.

60
00:04:33.583 --> 00:04:40.529
In Cambodia, indigenous peoples such as the Bunong maintain spirit forests in their ancestral lands.

61
00:04:41.817 --> 00:04:50.689
These traditions grow out of animism and an indigenous cosmology in which humans, ancestors and nature are connected.

62
00:04:51.983 --> 00:04:57.965
Phnom Kulen, a sacred mountain, has been revered by Khmer people for more than a thousand years.

63
00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:06.555
Conservation researchers have reported that sacred sites frequently contain more biodiversity than surrounding land.

64
00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:17.152
Some scientists, however, caution against romanticising tradition, noting that sacred status alone cannot stop large-scale logging.

65
00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:26.092
Nevertheless, many experts now acknowledge the value of ecological spirituality and reverence for nature.

66
00:05:27.383 --> 00:05:34.689
Protecting biocultural diversity, they argue, means protecting languages and beliefs as well as species.

67
00:05:35.983 --> 00:05:38.868
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

68
00:05:39.168 --> 00:05:42.712
A forest believed to be home to guardian spirits is a blank.

69
00:05:43.012 --> 00:05:49.556
A, spirit forest. B, biocultural diversity. C, sacred mountain.

70
00:05:53.550 --> 00:05:56.490
The answer is A: spirit forest.

71
00:05:57.983 --> 00:06:00.738
Which reporting verb signals doubt about a claim?

72
00:06:01.038 --> 00:06:04.877
A, claim. B, show. C, demonstrate.

73
00:06:08.883 --> 00:06:10.929
The answer is A: claim.

74
00:06:12.417 --> 00:06:14.973
'Elders insist that...' suggests they blank.

75
00:06:15.273 --> 00:06:20.668
A, feel very strongly. B, are unsure. C, have changed their mind.

76
00:06:24.683 --> 00:06:28.123
The answer is A: feel very strongly.

77
00:06:29.617 --> 00:06:32.870
The belief that rivers and trees have spirits is blank.

78
00:06:33.170 --> 00:06:39.296
A, animism. B, ecological spirituality. C, indigenous cosmology.

79
00:06:43.283 --> 00:06:45.875
The answer is A: animism.

80
00:06:47.383 --> 00:06:51.217
According to the text, what do sacred sites frequently contain?

81
00:06:51.517 --> 00:06:58.004
A, more biodiversity. B, more tourists. C, fewer trees.

82
00:07:02.017 --> 00:07:05.967
The answer is A: more biodiversity.

83
00:07:07.483 --> 00:07:13.050
Now it's your turn. Part one: Can spiritual beliefs help protect the environment?

84
00:07:18.350 --> 00:07:25.040
Part two: Report at least two different views using precise reporting verbs, then give your own.

85
00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:44.757
Researchers have found that spirit forests are often better preserved. Elders insist that the forest belongs to the ancestors. Some scientists dismiss this, but I would argue that reverence for nature works alongside the law.

86
00:07:45.057 --> 00:07:48.102
That is a well-argued answer!

87
00:07:49.117 --> 00:07:55.194
Great work today! You learned eight new words and precise reporting and attribution (extended).

88
00:07:55.494 --> 00:08:00.306
Today's value is caring for nature. Care for plants, birds and our planet.

89
00:08:00.606 --> 00:08:04.280
See you in Unit thirty-three. Goodbye!

90
00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:06.895
Thank you, Ms. Sarah! Bye, everyone!

